# Mac outbound proxy (mandatory)

From this Mac, **every** connection to the public internet or the remote VPS must use:

`http://127.0.0.1:7897`

## Apply to

- `curl` / `wget` / `fetch` to non-localhost hosts (set `http_proxy` / `https_proxy` / `HTTP_PROXY` / `HTTPS_PROXY`)
- Git / GitHub (`git push`, `git fetch`, `gh`, etc.)
- Package installs that hit the network (pip, npm, etc.) when run on this Mac
- SSH / SCP / rsync to the VPS, via HTTP CONNECT, e.g.:

```bash
-o ProxyCommand='/usr/bin/nc -X connect -x 127.0.0.1:7897 %h %p'
```

Or a wrapper: `ProxyCommand='/path/to/ssh-proxy-7897.sh %h %p'` where the script runs  
`nc -X connect -x 127.0.0.1:7897 "$1" "$2"`.

- Mac Helper install/runtime: `--proxy http://127.0.0.1:7897` (or `HXYLIVE_PROXY_URL`)

## Do not proxy

- `127.0.0.1` / `localhost` only (Mac Helper `17899`, local health checks)

## Do not

- Open direct SSH/SCP/curl to the VPS or other WAN hosts without 7897
- Assume the sandbox “auto proxy” covers SSH — always set ProxyCommand explicitly for SSH/SCP
